-- Refresh the exercise pool from `data/exercise_pool/*.json` (2026-08-09, second pass).
--
-- Pool content ships as a full upsert every time rather than as hand-written deltas: the insert
-- below is generated by `scripts/build_exercise_pool.py --sql` and its `on conflict (slug) do
-- update` makes re-running it a no-op when nothing changed. An already-applied migration must not
-- be edited, so every later edit to the catalogue becomes another file exactly like this one, and
-- `test_migration_insert_matches_the_source_files` checks the NEWEST of them.
--
-- This pass restores one illustration: `overhead_db_triceps_extension` was shipped without a
-- picture because the source entry mapped to it draws a seated concentration curl — the
-- antagonist. `seated-triceps-press-with-dumbbell` is the same movement drawn correctly.
-- Two other entries stay unillustrated for good: the source repository itself serves
-- byte-identical files for `t-bar-rows` and `smith-machine-incline-bench-press` (both a
-- stability-ball plank), and one file for both frames of `hack-squat-machine`.
on conflict (slug) do update set
  names = excluded.names,
  instructions = excluded.instructions,
  aliases = excluded.aliases,
  match_keys = excluded.match_keys,
  category = excluded.category,
  movement_pattern = excluded.movement_pattern,
  primary_muscles = excluded.primary_muscles,
  secondary_muscles = excluded.secondary_muscles,
  tertiary_muscles = excluded.tertiary_muscles,
  equipment = excluded.equipment,
  is_unilateral = excluded.is_unilateral,
  long_length = excluded.long_length,
  dose_unit = excluded.dose_unit,
  default_rep_min = excluded.default_rep_min,
  default_rep_max = excluded.default_rep_max,
  default_rest_sec = excluded.default_rest_sec,
  tags = excluded.tags,
  image_url = excluded.image_url,
  image_urls = excluded.image_urls,
  image_license = excluded.image_license,
  image_attribution = excluded.image_attribution,
  updated_at = now();
